      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate at which the production $P(t)$ of the factory changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum number of units a factory worker can produce and the current production quantity. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum number of units a factory worker can produce, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=53\\text{ units},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k(53-P).\n$$"
